Dear Jubail Team,



Please support us regarding the materials that will be stored in the Jubail=
 warehouse.

Kindly coordinate directly with Mr. @Mohammed Mabrouk<mailto:mohammed.mabro=
uk@nesmainfrastructure.com> and provide him with the PO and DN in order to =
register the information of the received materials as required, and arrange=
 for a safety personnel if required.



Please take into consideration that we currently have only one piece of equ=
ipment there, which is a 10 ton forklift.

Therefore, I kindly request that the necessary action be taken to arrange a=
ny additional equipment for unloading materials in case the incoming materi=
als exceed 6 tons, issue the required job order, and coordinate its availab=
ility to avoid any delay in receiving the materials.



Dear Mr. @Hesham Ibrahim<mailto:hesham.ibrahim@nesmainfrastructure.com>,



Based on the above, I kindly request that you follow up closely with the su=
bcontractor responsible for the gravel works to complete the tasks assigned=
 to him.

The winter season has already begun, and we have already received winter wa=
rnings.

Combined with the quantity of materials being received, the situation may b=
ecome dangerous and difficult to control later.

Therefore, I kindly request your support to ensure the contractor completes=
 the assigned works "lighting and gravel" so that the materials remain safe=
 and are not exposed to any damage.



Best Regards,

Amr Elkholy



